\newlabel{fig:v4_comparison}{{10}{16}{Quantitative impact of board-family quarantine and $\mathcal {D}_{\mathrm {V4}}$ label repairs: (\textbf {a})~overall test $\mathrm {mAP}_{50}$ and $\mathrm {mAP}_{50:95}$ comparing legacy $\mathcal {D}_{\mathrm {clean}}$ Four-Model WBF ($68.74\%$) against frozen re-scoring on $\mathcal {D}_{\mathrm {V4}}$ ($51.56\%$) and retrained $\mathcal {D}_{\mathrm {V4}}$ models ($45.67\%$ at $1280\text { px}$, $52.07\%$ at $1536\text { px}$, and $54.06\%$ validation-calibrated WBF); (\textbf {b})~per-class $\mathrm {AP}_{50}$ showing the $18 \rightarrow 222$ Electrolytic Capacitor shift collapsing frozen legacy performance ($73.3\% \rightarrow 7.2\%$) and recovering under leak-isolated $\mathcal {D}_{\mathrm {V4}}$ ensembling ($41.8\%$, with IC reaching $78.1\%$)}{figure.caption.21}{}}
